Hey, y'all!  I recently discovered that a wand of undead turning will
resurrect a corpse.  Well, there is a use for this feature besides getting 
more experience out of the same monster.  If you kill a gray dragon and
it sadly doesn't leave behind its scales, zap the corpse with the WoUT 
and kill the bugger again until a) it leaves scales behind or b) the
corpse disappears or doesn't reanimate, in which case you curse the
dev. team.  I realized I could do this about 5 levels after I had killed
two gray dragons, neither of which left their scales behind . . .

I'm playing version 3.1, so other versions may differ in this regard . . .

Note: do not try this at home if your character is not adequately equipped
with the proper gear & weapons, else you may become dragon toast.
